866 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493866 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b2b5eda7-fc54-5354-9c43-01751b2546c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493448 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493547 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186493760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186493760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493885 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f3f4b001-3f5d-563e-a82a-efaf92b09aad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493967 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186493866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493967 #edb/ref 1069 "q-149493" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493967 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493967 #edb/ref 1071 "A volleyball school for children splits the players into three teams, team $1$, team $2,$ and team $3.$ \n\n- $44%$ of children are in team $1,$ and $23%$ of children in this team have been playing for over two years.\n\n- $32%$ of children are in team $2,$ and $26%$ of children in this team have been playing for over two years.\n\n- $24%$ of children are in team $3.$\n\nIf $7%$ of all children can play in the blocker position, $40%$ of children who can play as blockers have been playing for over two years, and $10%$ of children who have been playing for over two years can play as blockers, what is the probability that a randomly chosen child in team $3$ has been playing for over two years? Round your answer to $3$ decimal places." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493967 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "deb0627a-b1f4-5ecd-95e2-372ffa642f2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186493967 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $B$ be the event that a child can play in the blocker position, $I$ be the event that a child has been playing for over two years, and ${T}_{1},{T}_{2},{T}_{3}$ be the events that a child is in team $1,$ $2,$ or $3,$ respectively. \n\nLet's break down the information given in the problem statement:\n\n- From the bullet points, we have the following information:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & P({T}_{1})=0.44 &  & P(I|{T}_{1})=0.23 \\\\  & P({T}_{2})=0.32 &  & P(I|{T}_{2})=0.26 \\\\  & P({T}_{3})=0.24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe disjoint union ${T}_{1}⊔{T}_{2}⊔{T}_{3}$ covers the entire sample space, and we have\n\n$$\nP({T}_{1})+P({T}_{2})+P({T}_{3})=0.44+0.32+0.24=1.\n$$\n\n- Since $7%$ of children can play in the blocker position, we have\n\n$$\nP(B)=0.07.\n$$\n\n- Since $40%$ of children who can play as blockers have been playing for over two years, we have\n\n$$\nP(I|B)=0.4.\n$$\n\n- Since $10%$ of children who have been playing for over two years can play as blockers, we have\n\n$$\nP(B|I)=0.1.\n$$\n\nWe want to find the probability that a randomly chosen child in team 3 has been playing for over two years, which is represented as $P(I|{T}_{3}).$\n\nUsing Bayes' theorem combined with the law of total probability, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(B|I) & =\\frac{P(I|B)P(B)}{P(I)} \\\\ P(B|I) & =\\frac{P(I|B)P(B)}{P(I|{T}_{1})P({T}_{1})+P(I|{T}_{2})P({T}_{2})+P(I|{T}_{3})P({T}_{3})} \\\\ 0.1 & =\\frac{(0.4)(0.07)}{(0.23)(0.44)+(0.26)(0.32)+P(I|{T}_{3})(0.24)} \\\\ 0.1 & =\\frac{0.028}{0.1844+0.24P(I|{T}_{3})}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving this equation for $P(I|{T}_{3}),$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1(0.1844+0.24P(I|{T}_{3})) & =0.028 \\\\ 0.1844+0.24P(I|{T}_{3}) & =\\frac{0.028}{0.1} \\\\ 0.1844+0.24P(I|{T}_{3}) & =\\frac{7}{25} \\\\ 0.24P(I|{T}_{3}) & =\\frac{7}{25}-0.1844 \\\\ P(I|{T}_{3}) & =\\frac{1}{0.24}(\\frac{7}{25}-0.1844) \\\\ P(I|{T}_{3}) & ≈0.398\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." #edb/ref 17